<title>USA: U.S. HEADLINE STOCKS - Issues to watch - Dec 2.</title>
<headline>U.S. HEADLINE STOCKS - Issues to watch - Dec 2.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Stocks to watch this morning:</p>
<p>* HealthSouth Corp said it would acquire Health Images Inc in a $270 million deal. Health Images shareholders will receive 0.446 of a HealthSouth share for each share they own. HealthSouth closed on Friday at 37-5/8 and Health Images closed at 15-5/8.</p>
<p>* Trump Hotels &amp; Casino Resorts Inc said it ended talks with Rank Group Plc over Rank's plans to invest in Trump's Castle resort in Atlantic City. Trump Hotels closed at 14-1/8.  </p>
<p>* Loewen Group said a Texas court dismissed a lawsuit brought by Service Corp International. Loewen said the court action clears the way for it to pursue its anti-trust suit against Service Corp. Loewen is using the suit as a takeover defense. Service Corp closed at 30-1/8 and Loewen NYSE-listed shares closed at 40-3/8.</p>
<p>-- Wall Street desk, 212-859-1730</p>
